<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Türkçe.

  Natural Turkish rather than word-for-word English, because the alternative reads like a
  form filled in by a translator. Notes on the choices that are not obvious:

   * "Devam Et" for Continue, "Hikâyeyi Başlat" for entering a world. "Step in" is not a
     verb a Turkish player would recognise, so it became the thing the button does.
   * "Model hazır — ilk kullanımda yükleme yapılacak" for a model that is installed but not
     yet resident. It says both the good news and the wait, which is all the user needs.
   * "Yerel model" for a local model, because "yerel" is the ordinary word for something
     that lives on your phone.
   * Lowercase "s" in "modeller", because Turkish sentence case does not capitalise
     common nouns. Capitalising them is the single most common giveaway of a translated UI.
   * "Ayarlar", "Kitaplık" and "Dünyalar" are the words Turkish users actually use for
     settings, library and worlds - not transliterations of the English nouns.
-->
